- F-285 **In the components that the distance checks, the interpreter's library writes the static argument of every clause form whose big operator's bound names its parameter, of every list comprehension and of each `cond` call in `Condition`'s methods; `__bigOperator2`'s fused arm casts its result to `O0`.** The clause forms follow P-78. Those left unwritten are of plain-bounded big operators (`BIG ||`, `BIG AND`, `BIG OR`), which the checker takes at their bound, or of `BIG LEXICO`, which has no static parameter. The checker also infers an unwritten argument (F-364); the sites stay written. A `cond` call writes the call's result type, as `cond[\Maybe[\G\]\]`, since its branches answer a `Maybe`, a `Condition` or a `Generator`. The fused arm, the `typecase` arm that runs a nested big operator through `generate2`, casts its result to `O0`, its declared result type, so the checker does not type it `OR(I0,O0)` (row 632); this is the library's cast for an arm whose type a `typecase` cannot show (F-264). So the distance holds no site of these declarations (F-53). `PureList`, outside those components, writes none at its strided subscript, which under walk answers a list typed at its elements' run-time types, which a binding declared `List[\Shape\]` refuses (row 824). Tests: the distance stage; `tests/WrittenReductionArgumentsWalk`, `GeneratorDeclarations` and `NestedReductionFusion`, which run the arm fused; `PureListStridedSubscriptWalk`. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-body-arguments/REPORT.md`; `compile-ladder/rung-generator-slips/REPORT.md` section 5.
